\begin{abstract}
This paper presents contrastive analysis of deep learning for labeling kidney stones in medical images by utilizing and evaluating three neural network models Deep Neural Network (DNN), Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) and Autoencoder-based DNN (AE-DNN) on dataset of 9,416 kidney images from Kaggle \cite{kaggle2024kidney} as we assessed their performance using extensive clinical metrics. Practical results demonstrate that the MLP architecture achieved the highest accuracy of 99.67\% while AE-DNN showed competitive performance at 99.47\% accuracy. The study highlights contrastive analysis of ROC AUC (0.987 across all models) precision, recall characteristics and computational trade offs offering findings into architectural considerations for medical image classification and this research contributes to the understanding of deep learning applications in urological diagnostics while acknowledging their limitations including binary classification and the need for external validation.


\keywords{Kidney Stone Classification \and Deep Learning \and Medical Imaging \and Neural Networks \and Computer-Aided Diagnosis}
\end{abstract}



