\subsection{Experimental Setup}
\subsubsection{Training Configuration and Hyperparameters}
All models were trained using consistent framework with random seed initialization (seed = 42) for reproducibility. The Adam optimizer was employed with learning rate $\alpha = 0.001$ and default momentum parameters ($\beta_1 = 0.9$, $\beta_2 = 0.999$). Models were trained for 10 epochs with batch size 32, using categorical cross-entropy loss for classification:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}} = -\frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \sum_{c=1}^{2} y_{i,c} \log(\hat{y}_{i,c})
\end{equation}

For the AE-DNN autoencoder component, mean squared error loss was used during pre-training:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}_{\text{MSE}} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \|\mathbf{x}_i - \hat{\mathbf{x}}_i\|^2_2
\end{equation}

Learning rate scheduling with reduction on plateau (factor = 0.5, patience = 5 epochs) was incorporated to optimize convergence.


\subsubsection{Evaluation Metrics and Validation Strategy}
A comprehensive set of evaluation metrics was utilized to assess model performance from multiple perspectives. The primary metrics included accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score, calculated as follows:

\begin{equation}
\text{Accuracy} = \frac{TP + TN}{TP + TN + FP + FN}, \quad \text{Precision} = \frac{TP}{TP + FP}
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
\text{Recall} = \frac{TP}{TP + FN}, \quad \text{F1-Score} = 2 \times \frac{\text{Precision} \times \text{Recall}}{\text{Precision} + \text{Recall}}
\end{equation}

Additional clinical metrics included specificity and negative predictive value (NPV):

\begin{equation}
\text{Specificity} = \frac{TN}{TN + FP}, \quad \text{NPV} = \frac{TN}{TN + FN}
\end{equation}

The area under the Receiver Operating Characteristic curve (ROC AUC) and Precision-Recall curve (PR AUC) provided comprehensive measures of classification performance across all threshold values. Statistical metrics such as Cohen's Kappa and Matthews Correlation Coefficient (MCC) were also computed:

\begin{equation}
\kappa = \frac{p_o - p_e}{1 - p_e}, \quad \text{MCC} = \frac{TP \times TN - FP \times FN}{\sqrt{(TP+FP)(TP+FN)(TN+FP)(TN+FN)}}
\end{equation}

The validation strategy employed an 80-20 train-validation-test split with stratified sampling to maintain class distribution. Model selection was based on the performance of the validation set, with final evaluation conducted on the held-out test set.


